Android SDK License Acceptance Investigation & Fix Report
1. Root Cause Analysis
From the exact GitHub Actions log output:
Text
"7 of 8 SDK package licenses not accepted"
"Review licenses that have not been accepted (y/N)?"
"Accept? (y/N):"
The Trigger: The runner was executing android-actions/setup-android@v3. When it invoked Google's sdkmanager to install SDK packages, sdkmanager discovered 7 unaccepted Android SDK and Build-Tools licenses.
The Fatal Blocker: sdkmanager prompts interactively on standard input (stdin) asking (y/N)?. In a CI/CD environment like GitHub Actions, there is no interactive terminal or keyboard to send y. The process either freezes until the runner's 6-hour job timeout or immediately aborts with non-zero exit code when stdin closes.
Why it prevented later steps: Because setup-android exited with failure, GitHub Actions canceled all downstream steps (Build Android App Bundle, Sign Release AAB, Upload Artifact).
2. Implemented Fix
Eliminated the Conflicting Setup Action:
Removed android-actions/setup-android@v3 (which caused the interactive license prompt and sdkmanager version mismatch).
Added Non-Interactive License Acceptance:
Directly after actions/setup-java@v4, added an explicit non-interactive license acceptance step using yes | "$ANDROID_HOME/cmdline-tools/latest/bin/sdkmanager" --licenses.
The Unix yes command streams y continuously into sdkmanager's standard input, accepting all 8 SDK license agreements automatically in under 2 seconds without hanging or prompting.
